---
name: plan_memory
description: >
  The day's PLAN memory seeded onto each Smallville persona at t=0
  (backend/smallville_agents.py, attach_agents). It is the agent's own private
  intention -- "go to <destination> and <activity>", plus the day's full
  itinerary -- distinct from its persona, so retrieval has the agent's whole plan
  to surface from turn 0 and the PLAN memory kind is exercised. The deterministic
  mock brain never reads it (it decides from location alone); real retrieval would
  surface it.
inputs:
  destination:
    type: string
    description: The first place the persona plans to go, e.g. "Hobbs Cafe".
  activity:
    type: string
    description: What the persona plans to do there, e.g. "tending the cafe counter".
  itinerary:
    type: string
    description: >
      The whole day's stops, pre-joined as "<activity> at <place>, then ..."
      (see attach_agents). Optional; the "Today's stops" sentence is dropped when
      it's empty.
sample:
  destination: Hobbs Cafe
  activity: tending the cafe counter
  itinerary: tending the cafe counter at Hobbs Cafe, then reading at the library
---
Plan: go to {{ destination }} and {{ activity }}.{% if itinerary %} Today's stops: {{ itinerary }}.{% endif %}
